## Lemma Target
Finite audited form:
  For exactly the seven HYP-3472 random projection-edge exceptions,
  every blocker label touched by every low-rank E/branch gate is private
  to a single dead component.  Therefore no union of adjacent E/branch
  gate labels, of any size, can delete a dead-cover projection edge.
  HYP-3476's pair failure is not a two-gate accident; it is an
  all-union private-label firewall for this carrier.
  The AP currentless rows are non-private and already close by the
  HYP-3476 two-gate pair-current terminal.  The only private firewall row
  with hard mirror debt is random_covering_031; the other six private
  rows are small-touch/no-hard packets.

